If transposing, play the transposed root chord for the (CaddG) and add the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  The intro begins with a haunting piano piece.  You can emulate this by playing (Em)(C) and (D) and then do the guitar part.  Or you can pick out the individual notes and then do the guitar part.  Here's how to play the notes.  Just go slow and do it a few times first:

     Part one, 8 notes:  Form (Em) with your middle and ring finger (you'll never come off the (Em) but will slide up from the 2nd fret to the 4th fret and back to the 2nd fret).  Pick the 5th string (b) and the 4th string (e), still holding the (Em) form slide up to the 4th fret and pick the 4th string (f#), slide back down and pick the open 3rd string (g), add your pinky to the 3rd string/2nd fret and pick the 3rd string (a), lift off and pick the now open 3rd string (g), slide back up to the 4th fret and pick the 4th string (f#), slide down and pick the 4th string (e).

     Part two, 6 notes:  Form (C) and pick the 5th (c), 4th (e), and 3rd strings (g), bring your ring finger down to form (Am) and pick the covered 3rd string (a), lift off the index finger and pick the open 2nd string (b), lift off the ring finger and pick the open 3rd string (g).

     Part three, 8 notes:  Form (D) and pick the 4th string (d) and then the 3rd string (e), lift off all fingers and pick the open 2nd string (b), cover the 2nd string/1st fret with your index finger and pick it (c), lift off and pick the now open 2nd string again (b), pick the open 3rd string (g), cover the 3rd string/3rd fret and pick it (a), lift off and pick the now open 3rd string again (g).
     
     Finish with four strums of (G) four times, pause briefly, and then strum (G) once and (CaddG) once.  Do it again.  Finish with three strums of (G) and one strum of |D|-|C|-|G|.

TIP:  The (CaddG) will be easier to play if you play (G) with your pinky on the 1st string instead of the ring finger.  That way you can pivot from (G) to (C) while keeping the pinky anchored.  And if too difficult just play (C) without the pinky. 
      

